---
// The closing statement. On wide screens the section is two and a half screens tall and its content
// sticks, so the scroll has time to play the picture beside it: the page turns dark, the chrome is
// a scatter of loose drops (stop "chaos") that flow together into one perfect sphere (stop "order").
---

<section id="closing" class="closing" data-stop="chaos" data-stop-late="order">
  <div class="closing-sticky">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="closing-text">
        <p class="label">Why a person, not just a prompt</p>
        <h2 class="heading mt-6" data-split>Experience decides what to build.</h2>
        <div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 reveal">
          <p class="lead">AI writes code fast, and I use it every day. It does not know your business, what breaks in production at night, or which shortcut costs you a year later.</p>
          <p class="lead">Someone who has shipped it before builds it in a fraction of the time, with fewer surprises, and leaves you a system you can still run in five years.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .closing {
    padding-block: 7rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .closing-text {
      max-width: 56%;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) and (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .closing {
      height: 250vh;
      padding-block: 0;
    }
    .closing-sticky {
      position: sticky;
      top: 0;
      height: 100dvh;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
    }
  }
</style>
